---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { content } from '../../data/content';

const t = content.en;
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy — Google Play build — Munadi"
  description="How the Google Play build of Munadi handles data: no accounts, ads, analytics, or trackers. Approximate location is used only for Qibla, the place name, and the prayer-time area."
>
  <Header
    lang="en"
    t={t}
    home="/"
    alternatePath="/ar/privacy/play/"
    showDownload={false}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="document-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy · Google Play</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p>
          Munadi is a simple, offline prayer-times app that began in Qatar.
          This policy covers the <strong>Google Play build</strong> of Munadi, the
          version installed and updated by Google Play. It has no internet permission.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container">
      <article class="document">
        <p class="effective">Effective: 8 November 2026</p>

        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No accounts, ads, analytics, or trackers.</li>
          <li>Prayer times and settings stay on your device.</li>
          <li>
            Approximate location is used for the Qibla compass, the place name, and the
            prayer-time area.
          </li>
          <li>The app has no internet permission and sends no data to us.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data the app uses</h2>

        <h3>Approximate location</h3>
        <p>
          Munadi requests <strong>approximate location only</strong>; precise location
          is not requested. It is used to calculate the Qibla direction and distance,
          show a place name, and suggest the nearest prayer-time area. The last
          approximate location and place are cached in the app’s private storage so the
          Qibla screen can open quickly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Place names are matched on the device from a built-in list. When location is
          already allowed, the app may check it at launch to suggest an area. Your
          location is not sent anywhere.
        </p>
        <p>
          On first launch, Munadi also reads which country your mobile network and SIM
          card belong to, without any permission, only to open the right country in the
          city list. This stays on your device. Location may suggest the nearest listed
          city in any region, and never switches it for you.
        </p>

        <h3>Settings and timetable</h3>
        <p>
          Theme, color, language, prayer-time city, Asr choice, Hijri date adjustment,
          iqamah adjustments, notification preferences, and sound choices are stored
          locally on your device.
        </p>
        <p>
          In Qatar, prayer times follow the Qatar Calendar House timetable, stored inside
          the app, using the Doha table by default. You can choose Abu Samra, Dukhan, or
          Al Shamal in Settings, and the app may suggest one when location is available.
        </p>
        <p>
          In other regions (currently Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Kuwait, Oman, and Pakistan), prayer times are calculated on your
          device from the coordinates of the city you choose in Settings, using an
          open-source calculation library. Nothing about the calculation leaves your
          device.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can export your settings to a file you choose and import it later. The
          file is saved where you put it; Munadi does not upload it.
        </p>

        <h3>Network access</h3>
        <p>
          The Google Play build does not request the internet permission. Google Play
          delivers app updates; the app itself never checks for, downloads, or installs
          an update.
        </p>

        <h3>Permissions</h3>
        <p>Depending on the features you use, the app may request:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Approximate location, for Qibla and the prayer-time area</li>
          <li>Notifications, for adhan and iqamah alerts</li>
          <li>Exact alarms, to keep prayer reminders on time</li>
          <li>Foreground media playback and vibration, for the adhan</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can decline optional permissions and still use the prayer timetable.</p>

        <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell or share your data. Munadi has no accounts and no analytics
          SDK. Local data remains until you clear the app’s storage or uninstall it.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Munadi is a general-audience prayer app and does not knowingly collect
          personal information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated. The effective date above will change when it does.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:munadi.prayer@gmail.com">munadi.prayer@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="note">
          <h3>This website</h3>
          <p>
            This site is a static page hosted on Vercel. It uses no cookies, analytics,
            or tracking scripts. Vercel processes standard request information — such
            as your IP address and user agent — to serve and protect the site, subject
            to Vercel’s privacy policy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer lang="en" t={t} home="/" showDownload={false} />
</Base>
